// toolbox/resources.cla: curated Resource Manager declarations, Task 7
// (mac-resident-clarusc phase). DELIBERATELY THIN, same discipline
// toolbox/files.cla's own header documents -- just the two routines
// `file.readResource`'s native implementation needs (GetHandleSize/
// HLock/HUnlock, also used here, already live in toolbox/memory.cla; no
// need to redeclare them in a second catalog file).
//
// Every trap word below is confirmed directly against Apple's own
// Universal Interfaces 3.4 (Retro68/InterfacesAndLibraries/Interfaces),
// per this repo's standing trap-verification rule (decode the inline
// words -- see toolbox/osutils.cla's Gestalt correction for why a
// `#pragma parameter` line or a third-party reconstruction alone is not
// enough).
//
//   Get1NamedResource  CIncludes/Resources.h:436-439:
//                       `EXTERN_API( Handle ) Get1NamedResource(ResType
//                       theType, ConstStr255Param name)
//                       ONEWORDINLINE(0xA820);` -- no `#pragma parameter`
//                       line at all (this is a Handle-CFM-style
//                       declaration, not a `#pragma parameter`-annotated
//                       inline glue) -- bit 11 SET (0xA820 & 0x0800 !=
//                       0) --> PASCAL convention: args pushed on the
//                       stack left to right (theType, then name), Handle
//                       result. Corroborated in AIncludes/Resources.a:478
//                       `_Get1NamedResource: OPWORD $A820`.
//   ReleaseResource     CIncludes/Resources.h:465-466:
//                       `EXTERN_API( void ) ReleaseResource(Handle
//                       theResource) ONEWORDINLINE(0xA9A3);` -- bit 11
//                       SET, pascal, void result, one Handle arg.
//                       Corroborated in AIncludes/Resources.a:514
//                       `_ReleaseResource: OPWORD $A9A3`.
//
// KNOWN HAZARD: `ReleaseResource`, called on the native (emit68k) lane
// after reading a resource under a heap already busy with prior traffic,
// was empirically found to hang the boot SOLID on real hardware (Task
// 7's own live-drive bisection -- see runtime/clarus/native.cla's
// natReadResource doc comment for the full trap-by-trap isolation, the
// same technique that root-caused the File Manager's own PBGetEOFSync/
// PBGetFInfoSync-before-write hangs). native.cla's own implementation
// works around this by never calling it. Root cause not pinned down;
// a caller of this catalog entry directly should be aware the same
// hang may reproduce under similar busy-heap conditions.
//
// `theType` (Get1NamedResource's ResType/OSType parameter) is a packed
// 4-character code, same convention as `file.writeText`'s type/creator
// (Chapter 12) -- callers pass an `int` (e.g. the packed 'CLFS' value
// `file.readResource`'s own native implementation uses,
// runtime/clarus/native.cla's natClfsType), not a `string`; this catalog
// declares the raw trap only; the friendly `file.readResource`/
// `file.writeRes` intrinsics (Chapter 12) are the abstraction most
// programs should reach for instead of calling these two directly.

external func Get1NamedResource(theType: int, name: ptr): ptr = trap 0xA820
external func ReleaseResource(theResource: ptr) = trap 0xA9A3
